<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via three-day system repurchases.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via three-day system repurchases.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system through three-day system repurchase agreements on Monday, a Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>Analysts had anticipated a temporary reserve addition but some had looked for an overnight operation.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at 5-3/4 percent, above the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target for the rate, at the time of the operation.</p>
<p>(( --North  American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679))</p>
</text>
